Apple today seeded the first betas of iOS 27.2, iPadOS 27.2, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macos-27/">macOS Golden Gate</a> 27.2, tvOS 27.2, and watchOS 27.2. The software comes a day after Apple provided the second betas to developers.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/iOS-27.2-Next-to-iPhone.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1065585" /><br/>
To get the new betas, you can sign up on <a href="https://beta.apple.com">Apple's beta testing website</a>. After you're signed up, the betas can be installed through the Software Update section in the Settings app on each device.<br/>
<br/>
iOS 27.2 includes the redesigned Health app that Apple introduced at its September iPhone event. It features new Insights and Longevity tabs with more insight into health and fitness data. There's also a Health Age feature that uses your metrics to determine your fitness age vs. your actual age.<br/>
<br/>
In the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/apple-tv/">Apple TV</a> app, there are new profile options, and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a> AI is now available in French, Japanese, Korean, Portuguese, and Spanish.<br/>
<br/>
